 To find $49^{-1} \pmod{78}$, notice that $7^{-1} \equiv 55 \pmod{78}$, which means $7 \cdot 55 \equiv 1 \pmod{78}$. 

Now, since $49 = 7^2$, we can square both sides of $7^{-1} \equiv 55 \pmod{78}$. 

$$
\begin{align*}
49 \cdot (7^{-1})^2 &\equiv 1^2 \pmod{78} \\
49 \cdot 55^2 &\equiv 1 \pmod{78}
\end{align*}
$$

This gives us a candidate for $49^{-1}$ as $55^2$. 

To verify this, calculate $55^2$ modulo $78$:

$$
\begin{align*}
(55^2) \bmod{78} &= (55 \cdot 55) \bmod{78} \\
&= 3025 \bmod{78} \\
&= 29 \bmod{78}
\end{align*}
$$

Since $49 \cdot 29 \equiv 1 \pmod{78}$, the solution $49^{-1} \pmod{78}$ is indeed $29$.

